      "note": "THE DOOR NOW RUNS WHAT IT IS HANDED. write_verdict extracts a runnable command from each criterion's instrument or refuses BY NAME quoting the prose it could not run; runs it under a bound; reads the chart's own declared expect_exit ahead of the builder's answer; refuses a contradicted outcome in BOTH directions (a reported pass the re-run disagrees with, and a reported fail the re-run reproduces as passing); refuses a bound overrun as a TIMEOUT by that name; and stamps the command, exit and output tail into the artifact before the digest is taken, so the berth's filename still describes its contents.\n\nTHE ORDERING IS THE DISTINCTION WORTH KEEPING. The run entries fire BEFORE the coverage check, which costs a fork on an artifact that was going to be refused anyway. What it buys is that a builder can tell \"go fix the build\" (the coverage kick-back over a reported failure) from \"your report of a failure cannot be reproduced and the build may be fine\". Those two send a builder to opposite work, and Law 7 forbids a diagnostic surface collapsing them into one shape.\n\nTHREE FINDINGS AGAINST THE INSTRUMENTS, ALL FIXED INSIDE THE VOYAGE. The first hollow reading was teeth_that_ran_at_all: 0 because the proof from-imported three names the reverted verdict.py does not carry, so the module died at collection and nothing was attributable — the ticket's own defect one level up. The names now ride the module. The second was 0 again because the proof's __main__ ran pytest.main and printed dots, so the seal read teeth_green: [] — it now calls the shared print_teeth_main. The third was four RECORDS in the decompose berth's writes_to reading as hollow; records cannot be pinned by any proof, so hollow gained a SKIP_RECORD class (commit a562d76) under ruling 2026-09-09-a-bug-the-voyage-uncovers-is-fixed-by-that-voyage. Measured through hollow's own resolver: 34 of 194 tickets (17%) carry a record in writes_to — a standing tax on honest charting, not this ticket's slip.\n\nCLOSE: all 8 validate criteria pass, run by the door itself (the live fire of this very build). hollow reads 2 measured, 0 hollow. determinism still reads the machine PURE DETERMINISTIC and REFUSES GATE.\n\nAND THE VOYAGE'S LAST FINDING IS ABOUT ITS OWN RECORD. The first run at this crossing was refused twice for naming test_chart_verdict.py and test_falsifier_verdict.py in `also_proven_by` — they were run green as criterion 6's regression check, but the coverage rung reads that field as a claim that a proof COVERS the boat, and neither does. Writing PROVES entries into them to get past the gate would have manufactured coverage, so the record was corrected instead: a retreat to TICKETME and a re-crossed BUILDME, which is the cut `crossings.proven_by_since_buildme` calls the whole of the kick-back protection. Nothing in the tree changed on the retreat. The finding worth keeping is that nothing at the PROVEME crossing tells a builder `also_proven_by` is a coverage claim rather than a log of what was run — the field name reads like the second thing, and the gate catches it four crossings later.",
